.TH "PB-TUNNEL-DOMAIN-VERIFY" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-domain-verify - Verify a tunnel domain


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel domain verify <tunnel> <domain> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify a tunnel domain

.PP
Check DNS ownership for one registered domain and update its verification state. --wait observes the operation; serving still depends on route and connector readiness.

.PP
Custom domains require DNS ownership verification before they can serve a route. Domain changes are scoped to one tunnel, and verification status is separate from route readiness. The instructions command returns the required authoritative DNS records.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for verify

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel-domain(1)\fP
